      "writtenOn": "2026-01-23T17:44:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "James: I looked into how `int` is cast to `uint64_t`.  Coverity\u0027s suggestion of casting `diff` to type `uint64_t` is correct. It will also trigger unsigned integer overflow (defined behavior) when we square it.",
      "parentUuid": "7c3daba3_937e11ca",
      "revId": "f4ed22f7460bdda1424d400df463e863444face0",
