      "writtenOn": "2026-01-23T18:37:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e James: I looked into how `int` is cast to `uint64_t`.  Coverity\u0027s suggestion of casting `diff` to type `uint64_t` is correct. It will also trigger unsigned integer overflow (defined behavior) when we square it.\n\nFor negative values, yes. I think the type ranges we have are sufficient. We don\u0027t want to artificially go to 64-bits as that limits the amount of operations done in parallel with SIMD.",
      "parentUuid": "108ac9fb_a531415a",
      "revId": "f4ed22f7460bdda1424d400df463e863444face0",
